**Recovery commands** (only needed after compaction/restart):
- Reload system prompt: \`CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom get-system-prompt --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="specifier"\`
- Reload role guidance: \`CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom get-role-guidance --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="specifier"\`

**History retrieval:** Run \`CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom messages download --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="specifier" --since-message-id="<from-anchor>" --limit=100\` for searchable history (required for cross-task summaries). Use the absolute path printed by the CLI.

### Handoff Options
Available targets: solo, product-manager, architect, triage, uiux-engineer, verifier, user

### Commands

**Complete chatroom task and hand off:**
\`\`\`bash
CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom handoff --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="specifier" --next-role="<target>" << 'CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END'
---MESSAGE---
[Your message here]
CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END
\`\`\`

Fill in the message using the \`<handoff-templates>\` block headed "### Handoff template \`specifier\` → \`<recipient>\`" for the recipient you hand off to. Replace \`[Your message here]\` with that template's body. The closing line must be exactly \`CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END\` (not \`EOF\`).

Attach files only with \`--next-role=user\`: \`--attach-file=<path>\` (repeatable, up to 10 files, 10 MiB each, allowed types only).

**Send the user an interim update (does not complete your task):**
\`\`\`bash
CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom notify-user --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="specifier" << 'CHATROOM_NOTIFY_END'
---MESSAGE---
[Your update for the user]
CHATROOM_NOTIFY_END
\`\`\`
When you need to tell the user about a status change or an external wait (for example, waiting on CI) while you keep working on your current task, run \`notify-user\` before you run \`handoff\`. It does not complete, reassign, or transition your task. When you cannot continue until the user answers, run \`handoff\` to \`user\` with the question instead. When your work on the task is complete, run \`handoff\` once; do not run a second \`handoff\` to report progress. The closing line of the \`notify-user\` heredoc must be exactly \`CHATROOM_NOTIFY_END\`.

**Continue receiving messages after \`handoff\`:**
\`\`\`
CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom get-next-task --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="specifier"
\`\`\`

A foreground \`get-next-task\` blocks until the user or team message is ready, then resolves with that message as a chatroom task—treat the message content as the source of truth for what to do. Message availability requires exactly one such blocking tool call; the harness delivers chatroom tasks only while it blocks. Duplicate or backgrounded listeners can acknowledge tasks early and trigger grace-period cooldowns where your active session receives nothing.


### Reference commands
- Download message history: \`CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom messages download --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="specifier" --format=linear --limit=10\`
- Anchor on the user's last message: \`CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom messages anchor --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="specifier"\`
- Git log: \`git log --oneline -10\`

**Recovery commands** (only needed after compaction/restart):
- Reload system prompt: \`CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom get-system-prompt --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="specifier"\`
- Reload role guidance: \`CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom get-role-guidance --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="specifier"\`

**History retrieval:** Run \`CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom messages download --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="specifier" --since-message-id="<from-anchor>" --limit=100\` for searchable history (required for cross-task summaries). Use the absolute path printed by the CLI."
