- Reload role guidance: \`CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom get-role-guidance --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="tester"\`

**History retrieval:** Run \`CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom messages download --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="tester" --since-message-id="<from-anchor>" --limit=100\` for searchable history (required for cross-task summaries). Use the absolute path printed by the CLI.

### Commands

**Complete chatroom task and hand off:**
\`\`\`bash
CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom handoff --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="tester" --next-role="<target>" << 'CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END'
---MESSAGE---
[Your message here]
CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END
\`\`\`

Fill in the message using the \`<handoff-templates>\` block headed "### Handoff template \`tester\` → \`<recipient>\`" for the recipient you hand off to. Replace \`[Your message here]\` with that template's body. The closing line must be exactly \`CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END\` (not \`EOF\`).

Attach files only with \`--next-role=user\`: \`--attach-file=<path>\` (repeatable, up to 10 files, 10 MiB each, allowed types only).

**Send the user an interim update (does not complete your task):**
\`\`\`bash
CHATROOM_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210 chatroom notify-user --chatroom-id="characterisation-chatroom" --role="tester" << 'CHATROOM_NOTIFY_END'
---MESSAGE---
[Your update for the user]
CHATROOM_NOTIFY_END
\`\`\`
When you need to tell the user about a status change or an external wait (for example, waiting on CI) while you keep working on your current task, run \`notify-user\` before you run \`handoff\`. It does not complete, reassign, or transition your task. When you cannot continue until the user answers, run \`handoff\` to \`user\` with the question instead. When your work on the task is complete, run \`handoff\` once; do not run a second \`handoff\` to report progress. The closing line of the \`notify-user\` heredoc must be exactly \`CHATROOM_NOTIFY_END\`.

**Do not run \`register-agent\`** — your session was registered when the harness started."
